@using Odyssey.Dtos.Finance

@*
    OdsTagIconPicker — the transaction-tag icon chooser (Odyssey Design System · components/TagIconPicker).

    A closed grid of the TransactionTagIcons catalogue, not a search over the Material set: a tag's
    icon is a key from the fixed list the API validates against, so the picker offers exactly that
    list and nothing the server would refuse. The catalogue is the shared Odyssey.Dtos declaration,
    never a client copy.

    The first cell is always Default — value null, drawn with the generic tag glyph inside a dashed
    outline. The API never stores the default key, so the picker emits null for it, and it treats any
    unknown or stale value as Default, mirroring the server's read-side projection.

    ARIA radiogroup with a roving tab stop: arrows move in two dimensions over the live column count,
    Home/End jump, selection follows focus (the radio pattern). icon-picker.js keeps those keys from
    scrolling the dialog and reports the column count. The caption names the selection in words and
    previews the label of the cell under the pointer or focus, so meaning never rests on the glyph.

    Keys render only as text inside a material-icons span — never MarkupString, never a class or style
    fragment (issue #279 security review).
*@

<div class="@RootClass">
    <div class="odc-iconpick-grid" role="radiogroup" id="@_groupId"
         aria-label="@(AriaLabelledBy is null ? AriaLabel : null)" aria-labelledby="@AriaLabelledBy"
         aria-describedby="@AriaDescribedBy"
         @ref="_grid" @onmouseleave="() => _peek = null">
        @for (var i = 0; i < _cells.Count; i++)
        {
            var index = i;
            var cell = _cells[index];
            var active = index == SelectedIndex;
            var isDefault = cell.Key is null;
            <button type="button" role="radio" data-idx="@index"
                    @key="@(cell.Key ?? "__default")"
                    @ref="_buttons[index]"
                    aria-checked="@(active ? "true" : "false")"
                    aria-label="@(isDefault ? "Default (tag icon)" : cell.Label)"
                    disabled="@Disabled"
                    tabindex="@(active ? 0 : -1)"
                    class="@CellClass(active, isDefault)"
                    @onclick="() => PickAsync(index)"
                    @onkeydown="e => OnKeyDownAsync(e, index)"
                    @onmouseenter="() => _peek = index"
                    @onfocus="() => _peek = index"
                    @onblur="() => _peek = null">
                <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">@(cell.Key ?? TransactionTagIcons.Default)</span>
                @if (active)
                {
                    <span class="odc-iconpick-check" aria-hidden="true"><span class="material-icons">check</span></span>
                }
            </button>
        }
    </div>
    <div class="odc-iconpick-caption" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="odc-iconpick-sel">
            <span class="material-icons">@(Selected.Key ?? TransactionTagIcons.Default)</span>
            <span>@(Selected.Key is null ? "Default" : Selected.Label)</span>
            @if (Selected.Key is null)
            {
                <span class="odc-iconpick-sub">the tag icon</span>
            }
        </span>
        @if (Peeked is { } peeked)
        {
            <span class="odc-iconpick-peek">
                <span class="material-icons">@(peeked.Key ?? TransactionTagIcons.Default)</span>
                <span>@(peeked.Key is null ? "Default" : peeked.Label)</span>
            </span>
        }
    </div>
</div>
